'''trapezohedral''' (trạ̄-pē-zọ̄-hē′drạl), ''a.'' [< ''trapezohedr(on)'' + ''-al.''] In ''crystal.'', pertaining to or having the form of a trapezohedron.—'''Trapezohedral hemihedrism, tetartohedrism.''' {{smaller|See the nouns.}}

'''trapezohedron''' (trạ̄-pē-zọ̄-hē′dro̤n), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. τράπεζα, a table, a trapezium base, + ἕδρα, a seat, side.] 1. In ''crystal.'', a solid belonging to the isometric system.

